# RLS and definers

`auth.uid()` is null inside some `SECURITY DEFINER` bodies. Use `request_user_id()`. Always set `search_path`.

```sql
-- ❌ BAD
uid uuid := auth.uid();

-- ✅ GOOD
uid uuid := public.request_user_id();
-- and: set search_path = public, auth
```

- Do not weaken RLS to make the client compile. Do not `GRANT` new definer functions to `anon` unless that is the explicit design.
- Clients must not write `stream_upload_claims`. Service role / Next Stream routes only.
- Video reads must keep `user_blocks`, hidden creators, and jam-gate (`048`) behavior.
- `lib/supabase-admin.ts` is server-only. Never import it from `screens/`, `components/`, or the Expo client.
- New definers: list who may `EXECUTE` them and why. Do not turn `row_security` off unless the function validates ownership the way `publish_own_video` does.
- Reports (`content_reports`) are insert/select-own today. Do not add a public “fetch all reports” RPC.
